<title>BELGIUM: Delhaize bolstered by Thai deal.</title>
<headline>Delhaize bolstered by Thai deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian retailer Delhaize &quot;Le Lion&quot; SA profited handsomely on Monday from news of a Thai supermarket chain venture, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1210 GMT, Delhaize was up 15 francs at 1,860, easily outperforming the Bel-20 index of leading shares which was down 0.38 percent.</p>
<p>Delhaize said the venture aimed to have over 100 stores in Thailand in five years' time.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
